{"words": [{"text": "قَدْ", "translation": "Indeed"}, {"text": "نَرَىٰ", "translation": "We see"}, {"text": "تَقَلُّبَ", "translation": "(the) turning"}, {"text": "وَجْهِكَ", "translation": "(of) your face"}, {"text": "فِى", "translation": "towards"}, {"text": "ٱلسَّمَآءِ ۖ", "translation": "the heaven"}, {"text": "فَلَنُوَلِّيَنَّكَ", "translation": "So We will surely turn you"}, {"text": "قِبْلَةًۭ", "translation": "(to the) direction of prayer"}, {"text": "تَرْضَىٰهَا ۚ", "translation": "you will be pleased with"}, {"text": "فَوَلِّ", "translation": "So turn"}, {"text": "وَجْهَكَ", "translation": "your face"}, {"text": "شَطْرَ", "translation": "towards the direction"}, {"text": "ٱلْمَسْجِدِ", "translation": "(of) Al-Masjid"}, {"text": "ٱلْحَرَامِ ۚ", "translation": "Al-Haraam"}, {"text": "وَحَيْثُ", "translation": "and wherever"}, {"text": "مَا", "translation": "that"}, {"text": "كُنتُمْ", "translation": "you are"}, {"text": "فَوَلُّوا۟", "translation": "[so] turn"}, {"text": "وُجُوهَكُمْ", "translation": "your faces"}, {"text": "شَطْرَهُۥ ۗ", "translation": "(in) its direction"}, {"text": "وَإِنَّ", "translation": "And indeed"}, {"text": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translation": "those who"}, {"text": "أُوتُوا۟", "translation": "were given"}, {"text": "ٱلْكِتَـٰبَ", "translation": "the Book"}, {"text": "لَيَعْلَمُونَ", "translation": "surely know"}, {"text": "أَنَّهُ", "translation": "that it"}, {"text": "ٱلْحَقُّ", "translation": "(is) the truth"}, {"text": "مِن", "translation": "from"}, {"text": "رَّبِّهِمْ ۗ", "translation": "their Lord"}, {"text": "وَمَا", "translation": "And not"}, {"text": "ٱللَّهُ", "translation": "(is) Allah"}, {"text": "بِغَـٰفِلٍ", "translation": "unaware"}, {"text": "عَمَّا", "translation": "of what"}, {"text": "يَعْمَلُونَ", "translation": "they do"}], "sahih": "We have certainly seen the turning of your face, [O Muḥammad], toward the heaven, and We will surely turn you to a qiblah with which you will be pleased. So turn your face [i.e., yourself] toward al-Masjid al-Ḥarām.1 And wherever you [believers] are, turn your faces [i.e., yourselves] toward it [in prayer]. Indeed, those who have been given the Scripture [i.e., the Jews and the Christians] well know that it is the truth from their Lord. And Allāh is not unaware of what they do."}